Here is a Unity C# script that sets the transform position, rotation and scale of whatever object it touches to 0 on all axes:

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

public class ResetTransform : MonoBehaviour 
{
  void OnCollisionEnter(Collision collision) 
  {
    collision.transform.position = Vector3.zero;
    collision.transform.rotation = Quaternion.identity; 
    collision.transform.localScale = Vector3.one;
  }
}
```

To use this:

- Attach this script to any GameObject in your Unity scene. 
- When this object collides with another object, it will call OnCollisionEnter(). 
- Inside OnCollisionEnter(), it gets the transform of the collision object and sets position to 0,0,0, rotation to no rotation, and scale to 1,1,1.

This will reset the transform of any object this touches back to default values.

